---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="How PerkCommons works" description="How PerkCommons reviews, publishes, and maintains open opportunity data.">
  <section class="container py-14"><p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand">How it works</p><h1 class="mt-2 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-semibold">A public index with a visible editorial trail.</h1><p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-8 text-muted">PerkCommons makes credible opportunities easier to discover while keeping the data portable, reviewable, and free.</p>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl rounded-md border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm leading-6 text-amber-950">This is the PerkCommons Next experimental fork. It demonstrates proposed architecture and policy changes; it is not the production PerkCommons service.</p>
    <ol class="mt-14 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-line bg-line md:grid-cols-5">{["Submit", "Screen", "Review", "Publish", "Maintain"].map((step, index) => <li class="bg-surface p-5"><span class="text-xs font-semibold text-brand">0{index + 1}</span><p class="mt-3 font-semibold">{step}</p></li>)}</ol>
    <div class="mt-16 grid gap-12 md:grid-cols-2">
      <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What review means</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">A moderator identifies a credible provider source, checks the claims recorded on the listing, and confirms the destination appears legitimate. New v2 records publish the claims checked, evidence purpose, review method, and next review date when available.</p><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">A source check is not a guarantee of acceptance, provider conduct, future availability, safety, or outcome. Providers control their programs and may change terms without notice.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">What belongs here</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Default discovery prioritizes selective, restricted, time-limited, materially valuable, or difficult-to-discover opportunities. Ordinary free products, public datasets, communities, and general memberships are classified as resources and should not crowd out opportunities.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Corrections and removals</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Anyone may report a broken link, expiry, incorrect claim, duplicate, scam concern, or privacy issue. Reports do not remove records automatically. A moderator records a decision; urgent tombstones can suppress a route while a validated Git change and static rebuild repair the public dataset.</p><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-muted">Disputed, sensitive, sponsor-related, and appealed decisions are intended to require an independent second reviewer.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Editorial independence</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Payment never purchases factual approval, verification, or removal of a competitor. Sponsored placements require an explicit public disclosure and remain subject to the same evidence standard.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Privacy boundaries</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Published factual records and their Git history are public. Contributor contact details, reporter details, private notes, assignments, and moderation research stay in the private workflow. Queue summaries deliberately omit private submission bodies and identities.</p></section>
      <section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">License and limitations</h2><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-muted">Structured public facts are intended to remain portable under the dataset license. Provider marketing copy should not be republished as PerkCommons editorial text. Legacy records still lack complete structured provenance, deadlines, and geography; the quality reports make those gaps visible rather than presenting them as verified facts.</p></section>
    </div>
    <section class="mt-16 border-t border-line pt-10"><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Accountability</h2><p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-7 text-muted">The experimental governance proposal covers reviewer independence, conflicts of interest, appeals, sponsorship, decision quorum, infrastructure access, and succession. Until those controls are adopted and tested, this fork must not be represented as production-ready community governance.</p><div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm font-medium"><a href="/trust/">Trust and transparency</a><a href="/privacy/">Privacy notice</a><a href="https://github.com/CodWasTaken/docs">Read experimental policies</a><a href="https://github.com/CodWasTaken/data/issues">Propose a correction</a><a href="https://github.com/CodWasTaken/site">Inspect the fork source</a></div></section>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>